                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Played through the first two levels as melee class.  I could understand this game being like it is if it was early access, but since it's not there's no reason for all the shortcomings.\n\nPros:\n-Good graphics\n-A decent attempt at classes/roles\n\nCons:\n-Game is utterly boring (I killed every non-boss enemy by simply teleporting to them... didn't even have to swing my sword)\n-Normal difficulty should be renamed extremely easy.  I never dropped below ~90% HP, and the arena was LITTERED with healing items.\n-Poor weaponization.  The first new weapons that you get from boss kills are worse than the weapons that you start the game with... SMH\n-Terrible hitboxes.  This may not be an issue for the spellcaster class, but for the melee class the mob hitboxes are nowhere near the actual mobs.\n-No Locomotion.  Yet another VR game with only teleport movement.",
